1
00:00:05,420 --> 00:00:07,540
Hey, hon? Would you help me get the plates down?

2
00:00:08,500 --> 00:00:11,620
Hey, here's an idea. Why don't we use our wedding china today?

3
00:00:11,800 --> 00:00:14,970
No, I think we should save our china for something really special.

4
00:00:15,140 --> 00:00:17,470
Like if the queen of England comes over.

5
00:00:18,050 --> 00:00:21,060
Honey, she keeps canceling on us. Take the hint.

6
00:00:22,180 --> 00:00:24,270
What if something breaks? They're expensive.

7
00:00:24,480 --> 00:00:27,520
What is the point of having them if we never use them?

8
00:00:27,690 --> 00:00:30,650
Okay. But if something breaks and then the queen comes over...

9
00:00:30,860 --> 00:00:34,490
I will explain it to her.

10
00:00:30,860 --> 00:00:34,490
Like I'd let you talk to the queen.

11
00:00:36,360 --> 00:00:39,450
The parade is really good this year.

12
00:00:39,620 --> 00:00:42,410
Man, those horses can crap.

13
00:00:43,080 --> 00:00:45,580
Next up is a marching band from Muskogee, Oklahoma.

14
00:00:45,750 --> 00:00:50,840
Muskogee? That's like four hours from Tulsa!

15
00:00:51,050 --> 00:00:53,960
Here's the float with the stars of the popular daytime soap...

16
00:00:54,170 --> 00:00:56,300
Days of our Lives.

17
00:00:59,510 --> 00:01:01,680
Oh, my God!

18
00:01:01,850 --> 00:01:04,430
Aren't you one of the stars of the popular daytime soap Days ofour Lives?

19
00:01:05,940 --> 00:01:08,890
I forgot! I'm supposed to be there!

20
00:01:10,190 --> 00:01:13,940
I can't believe I forgot! I usually write stuff like this down on my arm!

21
00:01:16,860 --> 00:01:19,480
Stupid long sleeves!

22
00:01:20,870 --> 00:01:23,740
What are you gonna do?

23
00:01:20,870 --> 00:01:23,740
I'll come up with a good reason...

24
00:01:23,910 --> 00:01:25,500
why I wasn't there.

25
00:01:25,660 --> 00:01:28,460
The producers are gonna be mad. They sat us down and said:

26
00:01:28,630 --> 00:01:33,670
"Everyone has to be there, 6 a.m. Sharp. That means you, Tribbiani."

27
00:01:33,840 --> 00:01:36,670
Like I was some kind of idiot.

28
00:01:38,550 --> 00:01:40,720
Well, you proved them wrong.

29
00:01:38,550 --> 00:01:40,720
Yeah.

30
00:02:31,060 --> 00:02:33,310
Oh, Emma.

31
00:02:33,480 --> 00:02:36,530
This is your first Thanksgiving.

32
00:02:36,690 --> 00:02:39,070
What are you thankful for?

33
00:02:39,240 --> 00:02:41,280
Mommy's boobies?

34
00:02:42,070 --> 00:02:44,780
A lot of people are thankful for those.

35
00:02:47,200 --> 00:02:49,120
Hello? Rachel?

36
00:02:49,330 --> 00:02:50,460
Who is it?

37
00:02:50,620 --> 00:02:53,710
It's your favorite sister.

38
00:02:53,880 --> 00:02:56,250
Jill?

39
00:02:53,880 --> 00:02:56,250
Amy!

40
00:02:56,460 --> 00:02:58,340
Hide my rings.

41
00:03:03,260 --> 00:03:06,470
Amy! Happy Thanksgiving.

42
00:03:11,310 --> 00:03:13,350
Do you have a hair straightener?

43
00:03:14,560 --> 00:03:16,350
Um... Hi.

44
00:03:17,730 --> 00:03:20,320
Hi.

45
00:03:17,730 --> 00:03:20,320
Hi.Hair straightener.

46
00:03:21,700 --> 00:03:25,320
I haven't seen you in, like, a year.

47
00:03:21,700 --> 00:03:25,320
I know. I've just been crazed.

48
00:03:25,530 --> 00:03:28,740
Well, me too. I had a baby.

49
00:03:29,370 --> 00:03:31,910
I decorated Dad's office.

50
00:03:32,830 --> 00:03:37,950
Yeah? Well, unless you pushed a desk out of your vagina, not the same thing.

51
00:03:39,970 --> 00:03:41,630
About that hair straightener, honey, I really need one.

52
00:03:41,800 --> 00:03:43,340
I'm gonna have dinner at my boyfriend's house.

53
00:03:45,600 --> 00:03:47,680
Oh, my God.

54
00:03:45,600 --> 00:03:47,680
Uh-huh.

55
00:03:47,850 --> 00:03:50,220
Is this Emmett?

56
00:03:53,900 --> 00:03:56,100
It's Emma.

57
00:03:56,310 --> 00:03:57,730
It's a girl?

58
00:03:59,650 --> 00:04:02,280
Hey, Amy.

59
00:03:59,650 --> 00:04:02,280
Amy, you remember Ross?

60
00:04:03,450 --> 00:04:05,310
Not really.

61
00:04:05,490 --> 00:04:09,200
But you are much cuter than that geeky guy she used to date.

62
00:04:12,080 --> 00:04:14,040
That was me.

63
00:04:14,540 --> 00:04:18,590
No, he was this creepy guy from high school who had this huge crush on her...

64
00:04:18,800 --> 00:04:20,630
since, like, the ninth grade.

65
00:04:20,800 --> 00:04:22,210
Still me.

66
00:04:23,050 --> 00:04:24,720
No, I'm not talking about you.

67
00:04:24,880 --> 00:04:27,720
It was your fat friend's brother with that bad Afro.

68
00:04:27,930 --> 00:04:31,930
Okay, Amy, I'm gonna save you some time, okay? All me!

69
00:04:36,940 --> 00:04:40,150
Careful. Careful.

70
00:04:40,440 --> 00:04:42,320
Careful!

71
00:04:42,690 --> 00:04:45,030
I'll tell you what. For the rest of our lives...

72
00:04:45,200 --> 00:04:47,610
I'll be careful until told otherwise.

73
00:04:49,780 --> 00:04:52,290
This isn't the china we picked out. MONICA: I know.

74
00:04:52,450 --> 00:04:55,830
After you left the store, I chose different ones.

75
00:04:56,460 --> 00:05:00,460
Why?

76
00:04:56,460 --> 00:05:00,460
Your taste is a little feminine for me.

77
00:05:00,670 --> 00:05:03,210
Suddenly flowers are feminine?

78
00:05:04,340 --> 00:05:07,260
Hey, everybody! Happy Thanksgiving!

79
00:05:07,470 --> 00:05:09,800
Happy Thanksgiving. Pheebs!

80
00:05:07,470 --> 00:05:09,800
What's going on, Joe?

81
00:05:09,970 --> 00:05:12,220
Listen, I need a good lie.

82
00:05:12,390 --> 00:05:13,770
Okay.

83
00:05:14,060 --> 00:05:18,060
How about the whole "man walking on the moon" thing, you know?

84
00:05:18,810 --> 00:05:22,110
You can see the strings, people!

85
00:05:22,320 --> 00:05:26,150
No, no, no. I need a good lie to explain why I wasn't at a work thing today.

86
00:05:26,360 --> 00:05:29,110
Honey, you stink at lying.

87
00:05:26,360 --> 00:05:29,110
I do not.

88
00:05:29,320 --> 00:05:32,660
Really? Let me ask you something. Yesterday at the coffeehouse...

89
00:05:32,830 --> 00:05:36,500
I went to the bathroom. When I came back, my muffin was gone. Who took it?

90
00:05:37,960 --> 00:05:40,170
Somebody opened the door to the coffeehouse...

91
00:05:40,340 --> 00:05:44,300
and a raccoon ran in and went straight for your muffin. I said:

92
00:05:44,460 --> 00:05:47,760
"Hey, don't eat that! That's Phoebe's!" And he said...

93
00:05:50,010 --> 00:05:53,810
He said, "Joey, you stink at lying." What am I gonna do?

94
00:05:53,970 --> 00:05:56,680
Don't worry. We'll come up with a lie. I'll help you.

95
00:05:56,890 --> 00:06:00,520
Great. That'd be great. Thank you.

96
00:05:56,890 --> 00:06:00,520
Sure. What was the work thing?

97
00:06:00,690 --> 00:06:02,150
Uh...

98
00:06:02,360 --> 00:06:05,440
"Pick up Grandma at the airport."

99
00:06:02,360 --> 00:06:05,440
Oh, man!

100
00:06:08,700 --> 00:06:10,990
She's precious.

101
00:06:11,490 --> 00:06:15,240
Do you ever worry that she's gonna get your real nose?

102
00:06:15,410 --> 00:06:17,330
Amy...

103
00:06:18,460 --> 00:06:20,830
Yes, I do. I really do.

104
00:06:25,250 --> 00:06:26,840
Hello?

105
00:06:27,010 --> 00:06:30,550
Yeah, hang on, one sec. Can I take this upstairs?

106
00:06:30,720 --> 00:06:32,970
Sure. We don't live there, but...

107
00:06:33,970 --> 00:06:37,930
Seriously? It's just these rooms?

108
00:06:38,640 --> 00:06:42,480
I thought you were a doctor.

109
00:06:38,640 --> 00:06:42,480
Yeah. No, Ross has a Ph.D.

110
00:06:42,730 --> 00:06:44,900
Ew!

111
00:06:48,240 --> 00:06:51,570
God, she is unbelievable.

112
00:06:51,780 --> 00:06:54,870
I know. I mean, a Ph.D. Is just as good as an MD.

113
00:06:55,080 --> 00:06:56,830
Sure, Ross, yeah!

114
00:06:56,990 --> 00:07:01,420
If I have a heart attack at a restaurant, I want you there with your fossil brush.

115
00:07:03,380 --> 00:07:05,460
Stupid Thanksgiving.

116
00:07:03,380 --> 00:07:05,460
What?

117
00:07:05,630 --> 00:07:08,800
What? What happened?

118
00:07:05,630 --> 00:07:08,800
My boyfriend canceled on me.

119
00:07:08,970 --> 00:07:11,470
I mean, I finally find a real relationship.

120
00:07:11,630 --> 00:07:16,600
Someone that I can spend this day with, and then his wife comes back into town!

121
00:07:16,760 --> 00:07:20,020
I swear, it's almost not even worth dating married guys.

122
00:07:20,480 --> 00:07:22,230
Don't say that.

123
00:07:23,650 --> 00:07:26,110
God, I was so looking forward to this.

124
00:07:26,270 --> 00:07:29,320
It was gonna be such a beautiful Thanksgiving.

125
00:07:29,490 --> 00:07:31,900
We were gonna have sushi.

126
00:07:32,990 --> 00:07:36,780
Amy, don't cry.

127
00:07:36,950 --> 00:07:38,920
Ross, can I talk to you in private?

128
00:07:38,920 --> 00:07:40,660
Sure, you wanna go upstairs, or?

129
00:07:45,540 --> 00:07:48,540
Look, I was thinking, if it's okay with Monica...

130
00:07:48,710 --> 00:07:51,300
I would like to invite Amy to Thanksgiving.

131
00:07:51,630 --> 00:07:54,790
I think that's a great idea. It'll be like the Pilgrims

132
00:07:54,790 --> 00:07:57,550
bringing the Indians syphilis.

133
00:07:58,890 --> 00:08:01,810
Look, I know she's a little tough to take.

134
00:08:01,980 --> 00:08:06,310
But she has nowhere else to go, and she's my sister. She's Emma's aunt.

135
00:08:06,480 --> 00:08:11,490
And I would like them to bond.

136
00:08:06,480 --> 00:08:11,490
I don't want them bonding too much.

137
00:08:11,650 --> 00:08:14,200
I don't want her telling Emma she needs a nose job.

138
00:08:14,410 --> 00:08:18,370
Ross, she may need one. We're just gonna have to make our peace with that!

139
00:08:25,750 --> 00:08:27,540
Hi!

140
00:08:25,750 --> 00:08:27,540
Hey.

141
00:08:27,710 --> 00:08:30,920
Hey, you guys. This is my sister Amy.

142
00:08:31,090 --> 00:08:34,550
This is Chandler, Joey, Phoebe, and you know Mon.

143
00:08:35,390 --> 00:08:36,880
Hi.

144
00:08:35,390 --> 00:08:36,880
Oh, my God.

145
00:08:37,050 --> 00:08:39,260
You're on Days of our Lives!

146
00:08:39,430 --> 00:08:40,810
Yeah.

147
00:08:40,970 --> 00:08:44,390
Wow! They must put a lot of makeup on you.

148
00:08:46,560 --> 00:08:48,900
Happy Thanksgiving.

149
00:08:49,940 --> 00:08:51,780
Hey

150
00:08:49,940 --> 00:08:51,780
Hi.

151
00:08:54,110 --> 00:08:57,160
So welcome. Is this the first time you're seeing Emma?

152
00:08:57,370 --> 00:09:00,490
Yeah, I think so. It's nice to meet you, Emma.

153
00:09:02,700 --> 00:09:06,040
Phoebe.

154
00:09:02,700 --> 00:09:06,040
That's a funny noise.

155
00:09:09,750 --> 00:09:13,590
Pheebs? I still need some help here.

156
00:09:09,750 --> 00:09:13,590
Right. Okay.

157
00:09:13,760 --> 00:09:18,180
So it's not just the lie you tell, but it's the way you tell it. For example...

158
00:09:18,340 --> 00:09:21,680
if you look at the ground when you talk, people know you're lying.

159
00:09:22,520 --> 00:09:26,550
I don't know why this is so hard for me. Lying is basically just acting...

160
00:09:26,730 --> 00:09:30,150
and I am a terrific actor.

161
00:09:26,730 --> 00:09:30,150
You are a terrific actor.

162
00:09:32,980 --> 00:09:36,900
Hey. Where's the baby?

163
00:09:32,980 --> 00:09:36,900
We just put her down for a nap.

164
00:09:37,070 --> 00:09:40,780
Listen, I was just thinking. You know what would be incredible?

165
00:09:40,990 --> 00:09:43,700
If you guys died!

166
00:09:45,000 --> 00:09:47,210
Thank you, Amy.

167
00:09:47,420 --> 00:09:50,250
No, no, then I would get the baby.

168
00:09:50,420 --> 00:09:54,750
It would be just like a movie. At first I wouldn't know what to do with her.

169
00:09:54,920 --> 00:09:59,050
And then I would rise to the occasion. Then I'd get a makeover and get married.

170
00:09:59,260 --> 00:10:01,600
That's a great movie!

171
00:10:03,140 --> 00:10:06,220
Yeah. Listen, not that you guys could stop me or anything...

172
00:10:06,430 --> 00:10:08,810
because, you know, you'd be dead.

173
00:10:08,980 --> 00:10:11,270
But I was thinking about changing her name.

174
00:10:11,440 --> 00:10:13,860
I'm just not really a big fan of Emily.

175
00:10:15,480 --> 00:10:17,110
Emma.

176
00:10:17,780 --> 00:10:19,780
Emma? Ross wants you.

177
00:10:22,120 --> 00:10:24,200
Phoebe!

178
00:10:25,490 --> 00:10:28,500
Why does she keep making that noise?

179
00:10:31,040 --> 00:10:33,380
Honey, I don't know how to tell you this...

180
00:10:33,540 --> 00:10:37,880
but if something were to happen to Ross or myself...

181
00:10:38,090 --> 00:10:41,340
you wouldn't get the baby.

182
00:10:38,090 --> 00:10:41,340
Well, who would?

183
00:10:42,010 --> 00:10:45,640
Well, we haven't officially asked them yet...

184
00:10:45,810 --> 00:10:48,520
but we would want Monica and Chandler.

185
00:10:48,680 --> 00:10:50,600
I can't believe you'd want us to raise Emma.

186
00:10:50,770 --> 00:10:53,060
Oh, my God, I'm so moved.

187
00:10:53,270 --> 00:10:55,940
I don't believe this. Hold on a second. You guys die...

188
00:10:56,110 --> 00:10:58,610
and I don't get your baby?

189
00:10:58,820 --> 00:11:02,160
Amy, see, we're a lot closer to Monica and Chandler.

190
00:11:02,320 --> 00:11:06,580
We see them every day. And truthfully, you don't seem connected to the baby.

191
00:11:06,790 --> 00:11:10,370
Connected? To what? She's a lump.

192
00:11:13,000 --> 00:11:15,840
You know, guys, I've gotta say this means so much to me.

193
00:11:16,050 --> 00:11:19,340
I mean, that you would trust me with your child.

194
00:11:19,510 --> 00:11:22,130
I mean, we all know that Monica and I have been...

195
00:11:22,300 --> 00:11:24,640
trying to have a baby of our own.

196
00:11:24,800 --> 00:11:30,020
You know, I've had my doubts about my skills as a father, but...

197
00:11:31,520 --> 00:11:33,600
That you two...

198
00:11:34,150 --> 00:11:37,270
That you two...

199
00:11:34,150 --> 00:11:37,270
This guy?

200
00:11:38,530 --> 00:11:40,070
Seriously?

201
00:11:45,490 --> 00:11:47,700
Okay, it's time for dinner.

202
00:11:47,870 --> 00:11:50,580
Everyone, we're using our fancy china...

203
00:11:50,750 --> 00:11:54,670
and it's very expensive, so please be careful.

204
00:11:55,960 --> 00:12:00,670
Whoa. Whoa. Whoa...

205
00:12:01,510 --> 00:12:05,220
Okay, just to be clear, comedy with the plates will not be well-received.

206
00:12:12,850 --> 00:12:14,640
Hey!

207
00:12:14,810 --> 00:12:18,730
How come my plate's less fancy than everyone else's?

208
00:12:19,860 --> 00:12:22,440
Do you not trust me with a fancy plate?

209
00:12:22,610 --> 00:12:25,740
No, honey. That's a special plate.

210
00:12:25,910 --> 00:12:29,620
See, it's a game. Whoever gets that plate wins.

211
00:12:31,160 --> 00:12:33,960
I can't believe I won!

212
00:12:34,920 --> 00:12:38,210
You know, this is such a slap in the face. I mean, I'm your sister...

213
00:12:38,380 --> 00:12:42,340
and you would give your baby to these strangers over me.

214
00:12:42,550 --> 00:12:45,050
Monica is Ross' sister.

215
00:12:45,590 --> 00:12:49,390
No, Ross' sister was really fat.

216
00:12:50,930 --> 00:12:52,350
That was me.

217
00:12:53,060 --> 00:12:57,520
No, she was this dorky girl in school who followed Rachel around like a puppy...

218
00:12:57,770 --> 00:13:00,060
Amy, you've got to stop doing that!

219
00:13:06,160 --> 00:13:09,030
Okay, listen, I know you're having a bit of a family crisis...

220
00:13:09,200 --> 00:13:11,790
but you don't have to take it out on the plates.

221
00:13:11,950 --> 00:13:14,790
I mean, in fact, I think that everyone...

222
00:13:14,960 --> 00:13:18,880
should cut their food like this:

223
00:13:21,170 --> 00:13:24,090
Now, see? This way, you protect the plates...

224
00:13:24,420 --> 00:13:26,340
and let's face it, you have fun.

225
00:13:28,090 --> 00:13:30,890
Okay, how about this? If you guys die...

226
00:13:31,060 --> 00:13:34,890
and the crazy plate lady dies...

227
00:13:35,810 --> 00:13:39,100
then do I get the baby?

228
00:13:35,810 --> 00:13:39,100
No, if crazy plate lady...

229
00:13:41,650 --> 00:13:45,690
If Monica dies, then I would get Emma. Right?

230
00:13:49,160 --> 00:13:51,450
Well, actually...

231
00:13:49,160 --> 00:13:51,450
Actually what?

232
00:13:52,160 --> 00:13:55,530
It's just... It's just that in that case...

233
00:13:55,700 --> 00:13:57,620
then Emma would go to my parents.

234
00:13:58,120 --> 00:14:00,250
What?

235
00:13:58,120 --> 00:14:00,250
Hurts, doesn't it?

236
00:14:03,800 --> 00:14:07,000
Who has to die for me to get her?

237
00:14:14,560 --> 00:14:17,850
So if Monica's not around, I'm not good enough to raise Emma?

238
00:14:18,060 --> 00:14:20,480
No, that is not what we're saying.

239
00:14:20,690 --> 00:14:22,400
Yeah, he's lying. He looked down.

240
00:14:24,940 --> 00:14:27,070
Well, what's wrong with me? Am I incompetent?

241
00:14:27,280 --> 00:14:30,860
Because I managed to survive whatever it is that killed the three of you!

242
00:14:33,620 --> 00:14:38,660
You're taking this the wrong way. We think you'll be a wonderful parent.

243
00:14:38,830 --> 00:14:42,500
It's just... You're more the, you know, fun parent.

244
00:14:42,670 --> 00:14:46,880
Yeah, and we wanna make sure Emma also has someone like Monica...

245
00:14:47,050 --> 00:14:48,920
who's more of a disciplinarian.

246
00:14:49,090 --> 00:14:51,970
Someone who can be firm and strict.

247
00:14:52,140 --> 00:14:54,720
That's not how you see me, is it?

248
00:14:55,810 --> 00:14:58,350
No, you're all about the fun.

249
00:15:04,520 --> 00:15:08,190
I may not know a lot about babies, but do you really think I'm not capable?

250
00:15:08,400 --> 00:15:11,110
No. You both are equally capable.

251
00:15:11,280 --> 00:15:13,870
It's just you're strongest when you're together.

252
00:15:14,070 --> 00:15:17,910
Okay. So if we both had Emma, and I died...

253
00:15:18,580 --> 00:15:20,290
she'd have to give her up.

254
00:15:20,920 --> 00:15:23,580
Sure. Monica would have to give her up.

255
00:15:24,170 --> 00:15:27,090
I lie better than that, right?

256
00:15:28,460 --> 00:15:32,430
Let me just get this straight. So my two friends die, I get Emma.

257
00:15:32,590 --> 00:15:36,680
Then my wife dies. Then Emma, the one tiny ray of hope left in my life...

258
00:15:36,850 --> 00:15:40,350
gets taken away from me?

259
00:15:36,850 --> 00:15:40,350
There's your movie.

260
00:15:44,020 --> 00:15:46,730
Hey, there you are.

261
00:15:46,900 --> 00:15:50,110
You disappeared after dinner.

262
00:15:46,900 --> 00:15:50,110
Did somebody miss me?

263
00:15:50,320 --> 00:15:53,240
Was there a child to raise poorly?

264
00:15:53,780 --> 00:15:55,990
Ross and Rachel don't know what they're saying.

265
00:15:56,200 --> 00:15:58,080
It's not like they're so responsible.

266
00:15:58,240 --> 00:16:02,710
Emma is a product of a bottle of merlot and a five-year-old condom.

267
00:16:04,540 --> 00:16:08,540
No, but they're right. I'm not a strong father figure, and I never will be.

268
00:16:08,750 --> 00:16:11,380
No, you learn these things. You grow into it.

269
00:16:11,630 --> 00:16:13,380
Yeah, but it's not who I am.

270
00:16:13,590 --> 00:16:18,720
Everything they said is exactly why I was worried about having a kid. And it's true.

271
00:16:18,890 --> 00:16:21,850
And look, everybody knows it.

272
00:16:18,890 --> 00:16:21,850
I don't know it.

273
00:16:22,020 --> 00:16:25,600
I wanna have a kid with you because I think you'll be an amazing dad.

274
00:16:25,770 --> 00:16:28,400
At the fun parts and at the hard parts.

275
00:16:28,610 --> 00:16:32,110
Well, can you picture me saying, "Go to your room, you're grounded"?

276
00:16:32,950 --> 00:16:35,310
Can you hear me say, "You're grounded"?

277
00:16:35,490 --> 00:16:37,950
You said that to me last week.

278
00:16:39,790 --> 00:16:43,290
How hard is it? "No shoes on the furniture!"

279
00:16:49,840 --> 00:16:53,960
The producer from Days left a message asking why I wasn't at the parade.

280
00:16:54,170 --> 00:16:58,340
They said everybody's really pissed off at me. And they all got to meet Santa!

281
00:17:00,010 --> 00:17:02,430
It's okay. I thought of the perfect lie for you.

282
00:17:02,640 --> 00:17:06,100
It's easy to remember, and it doesn't invite a lot of questions.

283
00:17:06,310 --> 00:17:10,150
You weren't at the parade, because you had a family emergency.

284
00:17:10,360 --> 00:17:12,900
I like that! Yeah!

285
00:17:13,070 --> 00:17:15,950
I wasn't at the parade, because I had a family emergency.

286
00:17:16,160 --> 00:17:17,200
What happened?

287
00:17:18,280 --> 00:17:21,370
My sister's raccoon came...

288
00:17:18,280 --> 00:17:21,370
No, nothing with a raccoon!

289
00:17:24,500 --> 00:17:27,330
Wait, what are you doing?

290
00:17:24,500 --> 00:17:27,330
Setting the table.

291
00:17:27,500 --> 00:17:30,880
We thought it might be nice to use the fancy china for dessert too.

292
00:17:31,550 --> 00:17:35,130
How nice. Maybe later we can all blow our noses on my wedding dress.

293
00:17:42,390 --> 00:17:44,720
Hey, dude, you okay? Sorry about before.

294
00:17:44,890 --> 00:17:49,100
That's okay. You're totally right. I don't know anything about disciplining a child.

295
00:17:49,270 --> 00:17:53,820
But it did hurt my feelings, and I want you to know that if I die...

296
00:17:53,980 --> 00:17:56,240
you don't get Joey.

297
00:18:10,000 --> 00:18:12,040
In case you hadn't noticed, I'm not talking to you.

298
00:18:15,170 --> 00:18:17,920
You know, this is just... This is classic Rachel.

299
00:18:18,130 --> 00:18:22,600
Right. Remember in high school when I died and didn't give you my baby?

300
00:18:25,180 --> 00:18:28,100
This might be my one chance to have a child, Rachel.

301
00:18:28,310 --> 00:18:31,350
I mean, you know that I have been so busy focusing on my career...

302
00:18:31,520 --> 00:18:35,610
What career?

303
00:18:31,520 --> 00:18:35,610
I'm a decorator.

304
00:18:35,820 --> 00:18:39,200
You decorate Dad's office and now you're a decorator?

305
00:18:39,360 --> 00:18:44,030
Okay, I went to the zoo yesterday, now I'm a koala bear.

306
00:18:46,870 --> 00:18:50,670
Why can't you ever be supportive?

307
00:18:46,870 --> 00:18:50,670
You want to talk supportive?

308
00:18:50,830 --> 00:18:54,630
You didn't come and visit me when I was in the hospital having the baby!

309
00:18:54,800 --> 00:18:58,800
You didn't come see me in the hospital when I was getting my lips done!

310
00:19:00,300 --> 00:19:02,460
I did the first time.

311
00:19:04,640 --> 00:19:08,100
You know what? You want to know why I am not giving Emily to you?

312
00:19:08,270 --> 00:19:10,690
Emma.

313
00:19:08,270 --> 00:19:10,690
Whose side are you on?!

314
00:19:12,060 --> 00:19:16,610
I'm not giving you Emma, because you can't handle the responsibility of a child.

315
00:19:16,860 --> 00:19:19,070
Well, how hard could it be? You do it.

316
00:19:19,280 --> 00:19:21,110
Ooh-hoo-hoo-hoo.

317
00:19:24,870 --> 00:19:28,160
You wanna know why you don't want me to have the baby?

318
00:19:28,330 --> 00:19:30,580
Because you don't want me to be happy.

319
00:19:30,750 --> 00:19:34,380
You have always been jealous of me.

320
00:19:30,750 --> 00:19:34,380
Jealous of what?

321
00:19:34,540 --> 00:19:38,250
Of your lack of responsibility? Your immaturity?

322
00:19:38,420 --> 00:19:41,420
Your total disregard for other people's feelings?

323
00:19:41,630 --> 00:19:43,970
To name a few.

324
00:19:45,850 --> 00:19:47,470
You've always been like this.

325
00:19:47,640 --> 00:19:51,060
You had to have everything, and I couldn't have anything.

326
00:19:51,230 --> 00:19:54,440
Like in junior high, when you stole Timmy from me.

327
00:19:54,610 --> 00:19:57,480
I mean, do you even realize how much that hurt me?

328
00:19:57,690 --> 00:20:00,150
Timmy was my boyfriend, and you made out with him!

329
00:20:00,360 --> 00:20:02,320
Come on, that was 20 years ago. Get over it.

330
00:20:03,740 --> 00:20:06,700
I cannot believe that I invited you here today!

331
00:20:06,870 --> 00:20:10,790
Yeah, well, you know what I cannot believe? That my so-called sister...

332
00:20:10,950 --> 00:20:15,790
gets a 30% discount from Ralph Lauren, and I still have to pay retail?

333
00:20:18,210 --> 00:20:19,750
It's 45.

334
00:20:21,130 --> 00:20:22,970
You bitch.

335
00:20:25,510 --> 00:20:27,470
You just think you're so perfect...

336
00:20:27,640 --> 00:20:31,350
with your new baby and your small apartment.

337
00:20:32,810 --> 00:20:37,310
Well, let me tell you something. Your baby isn't even that cute.

338
00:20:39,360 --> 00:20:43,070
Too far, Amy. Too far.

339
00:20:45,280 --> 00:20:47,320
You take that back.

340
00:20:45,280 --> 00:20:47,320
No.

341
00:20:47,530 --> 00:20:49,950
Take it back!

342
00:20:47,530 --> 00:20:49,950
No. What are you gonna do? Make me?

343
00:20:50,160 --> 00:20:53,080
Hey, man, I work out!

344
00:20:54,670 --> 00:20:56,580
So do I.

345
00:20:54,670 --> 00:20:56,580
I do Pilates.

346
00:20:56,790 --> 00:20:58,500
I do yoga.

347
00:20:56,790 --> 00:20:58,500
Bring it on!

348
00:20:59,040 --> 00:21:01,920
Put the plates in the boxes! Put the plates in the boxes!

349
00:21:04,380 --> 00:21:06,800
Did you just push me?

350
00:21:04,380 --> 00:21:06,800
Yeah, I think I did.

351
00:21:07,010 --> 00:21:08,300
All right, that's it.

352
00:21:08,510 --> 00:21:11,310
Forget the bubble wrap! There isn't time!

353
00:21:13,560 --> 00:21:15,350
Frizzy, frizzy, frizzy!

354
00:21:20,150 --> 00:21:22,810
Shouldn't we stop this?

355
00:21:20,150 --> 00:21:22,810
Are you out of your mind?

356
00:21:22,990 --> 00:21:25,360
Let's throw some Jell-O on them!

357
00:21:29,990 --> 00:21:31,650
Gross!

358
00:21:43,300 --> 00:21:48,300
All right, that is it! This is our apartment, and you cannot behave this way!

359
00:21:48,470 --> 00:21:51,220
If you can't act your age, you shouldn't be here at all.

360
00:21:51,430 --> 00:21:56,310
Those plates may not be as nice as the pretty pink ones that I picked out...

361
00:21:57,190 --> 00:22:02,270
but they're important to Monica. And I want you to apologize to her now.

362
00:22:02,520 --> 00:22:05,070
I'm sorry.

363
00:22:02,520 --> 00:22:05,070
Mon, I'm so sorry.

364
00:22:05,240 --> 00:22:07,150
Okay. That's better.

365
00:22:07,320 --> 00:22:10,700
Now, I want you to apologize to each other and mean it.

366
00:22:11,280 --> 00:22:12,700
Sorry.

367
00:22:11,280 --> 00:22:12,700
Sorry.

368
00:22:12,910 --> 00:22:16,250
By the way, that fight was totally arousing.

369
00:22:20,460 --> 00:22:22,380
Dude, well done.

370
00:22:22,590 --> 00:22:27,630
If I die and Rachel dies and Monica dies, you can totally take care of Emma.

371
00:22:28,340 --> 00:22:30,130
Yeah? Well, thanks.

372
00:22:30,640 --> 00:22:33,760
So... So now do I get Joey?

373
00:22:35,640 --> 00:22:40,480
Okay. But you should know he eats a lot and shoves pennies up his nose.

374
00:22:45,610 --> 00:22:47,780
Are you okay, Mon?

375
00:22:45,610 --> 00:22:47,780
Uh-huh.

376
00:22:47,940 --> 00:22:51,660
I mean, these things happen. I mean, it's just a plate.

377
00:22:51,820 --> 00:22:55,580
It's not like somebody died.

378
00:22:51,820 --> 00:22:55,580
It's all right. You can mourn.

379
00:22:55,950 --> 00:22:59,910
Thank you. It was so beautiful!

380
00:23:02,040 --> 00:23:04,290
I'm gonna go to Joey's and get the pies.

381
00:23:04,500 --> 00:23:08,260
Actually, not pies. It's just pie.

382
00:23:09,630 --> 00:23:11,840
I don't care.

383
00:23:12,010 --> 00:23:15,600
Oh, my God, I've lost the will to scold.

384
00:23:19,640 --> 00:23:21,770
Look, Amy...

385
00:23:22,230 --> 00:23:23,810
we got a little...

386
00:23:23,980 --> 00:23:26,820
a little out-of-control over there.

387
00:23:27,530 --> 00:23:28,980
And I'm sorry.

388
00:23:29,150 --> 00:23:31,740
You're my sister...

389
00:23:31,910 --> 00:23:34,320
and if it really means that much to you...

390
00:23:34,660 --> 00:23:37,620
So you're gonna give me the baby?

391
00:23:34,660 --> 00:23:37,620
No, I was...

392
00:23:37,790 --> 00:23:40,870
I was gonna let you use my Ralph Lauren discount.

393
00:23:42,250 --> 00:23:45,170
You are not gonna regret this.

394
00:23:48,050 --> 00:23:51,260
She needs changing.

395
00:23:48,050 --> 00:23:51,260
No, no, no. I'll get her.

396
00:23:51,470 --> 00:23:55,970
I am super confident, totally responsible and fourth in line to raise Emma.

397
00:23:56,140 --> 00:24:00,520
I'll be right there, Emma! Just let me get my trusty diaper bag here.

398
00:24:06,060 --> 00:24:09,150
Well, what do you know? I guess I'll be the one who dies first.

399
00:24:20,580 --> 00:24:24,250
Does Monica know about her plates? CHANDLER: Nope.

400
00:24:24,460 --> 00:24:25,960
Broke them all, huh?

401
00:24:24,460 --> 00:24:25,960
Yep.

402
00:24:26,170 --> 00:24:28,000
You gonna tell her?

403
00:24:26,170 --> 00:24:28,000
Nope.

404
00:24:30,090 --> 00:24:33,670
Hey. So I'm gonna put the plates back.

405
00:24:33,840 --> 00:24:37,390
I think you're right. We shouldn't use these plates for a long time.

406
00:24:37,600 --> 00:24:41,100
Like only if the queen comes?

407
00:24:37,600 --> 00:24:41,100
Maybe not even then.

408
00:24:42,140 --> 00:24:43,680
Hey. I did it.

409
00:24:43,890 --> 00:24:47,400
I told my producer I had a family emergency. He totally bought it.

410
00:24:47,560 --> 00:24:52,230
Thanks for teaching me how to lie.

411
00:24:47,560 --> 00:24:52,230
No problem. Next week, stealing.

412
00:24:53,610 --> 00:24:56,570
Bye, plates.

413
00:24:53,610 --> 00:24:56,570
You told her you broke all the plates?

414
00:24:58,910 --> 00:25:01,740
What?! Something happened with the plates?

415
00:25:03,370 --> 00:25:07,120
Yeah, this raccoon came in...

